# What this board does not have, on top of common/kernel.forbidden.
#
# The touch controller is the whole input device and the one USB port
# carries a camera, so the input and storage stacks a general-purpose
# computer needs are not built here. The stick board requires the same
# symbols, which is why they are in a board's file and not in a shared one.

HID            USB is kept for a webcam and for nothing else; no keyboard, no mouse, no keypad
USB_STORAGE    the only storage is the card the firmware booted from
SCSI           only USB storage would have wanted it
BCM_VCIO       /dev/vcio is the firmware mailbox from userspace, which is how vcgencmd burns the SoC's OTP

# Faraday (PLAN.md §4.2, §4.6).
FAT_FS        the card's FAT is read by faraday-disk, unprivileged, never by the kernel
VFAT_FS       as FAT_FS
MSDOS_FS      as FAT_FS
EXFAT_FS      a filesystem a card could carry, and nothing here reads it
ISO9660_FS    as EXFAT_FS
USB_PRINTER   a printer interface has nothing to bind to here
USB_MON       the USB traffic monitor has nothing to show anyone on a device that signs

# Faraday (PLAN.md §5.3): no process's memory is ever written to a file.
COREDUMP      a crash would write the app's memory, keys included, to a file
